# --- Local development (`npm run dev`) ---
# Vite loads `.env`, `.env.local`, and `.env.development` — it does NOT load
# `.env.production`. Put the same VITE_* values in `.env` (or `.env.development`)
# for local dev, e.g. `cp .env.production .env` once (`.env` is gitignored).

# --- Netlify (or any host): VITE_* is baked in at `npm run build` ---
# After changing variables in Netlify, trigger a new deploy (e.g. “Clear cache and deploy”).
# The live site will not update until a build runs with those values.

# --- GoDaddy static hosting (e.g. https://rslibrary.in) ---
# GoDaddy Linux/cPanel serves only the built files from `dist/`. Netlify Functions do NOT run.
#
# 1. Copy `.env.godaddy.example` → `.env.godaddy` and fill every `VITE_*` you need (same as production),
#    but do NOT set `VITE_CONTACT_SUBMIT_URL`. Keep `VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY` so the form posts
#    straight to Web3Forms from the browser. In Web3Forms, allow domain `rslibrary.in` if the dashboard asks.
# 2. Run: npm ci && npm run build:godaddy
# 3. Upload everything inside `dist/` into your domain’s document root (often `public_html` for the
#    primary domain, or the folder cPanel assigns for `rslibrary.in` if it is an addon domain).
# 4. DNS: point `rslibrary.in` (and optional `www`) to this hosting per GoDaddy’s DNS / cPanel docs.
# 5. Enable SSL in cPanel, then optionally uncomment the HTTPS lines in `public/.htaccess`.
# 6. If you later move back to Netlify only, keep using `npm run build` with Netlify env as before.

# --- Contact form (Web3Forms) ---
# Local dev: set the key here — the browser posts directly to api.web3forms.com.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=

# Netlify: the app prefers direct browser → Web3Forms whenever VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY is in the
# build (recommended for custom domains). Optional serverless proxy — only if you omit the VITE key
# from the client bundle:
#   1. Deploy this repo (includes netlify/functions/contact.mjs + redirect /api/contact).
#   2. In Netlify → Environment variables add:
#        VITE_CONTACT_SUBMIT_URL=/api/contact
#        WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=<same Access Key as in Web3Forms dashboard>
#   3. Clear cache and deploy.
#   4. Optional: remove VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY from Netlify if you only use the proxy.
# In Web3Forms dashboard → Settings, add BOTH `*.netlify.app` and your custom domain (e.g. rslibrary.in)
# under allowed / restricted domains if you use that feature (Pro).
#
# --- Custom domain on Netlify (e.g. rslibrary.in) — form OK but no email ---
# • Wait until DNS + SSL show as active on Netlify; flaky HTTPS during propagation can confuse testing.
# • Check Spam / Gmail Promotions for mail from web3forms.com; mark “Not spam” once so future mail lands in Primary.
# • Web3Forms may require you to contact them to approve a new custom domain (see their Troubleshooting:
#   “Form works locally, but not working on my hosted domain”).
# • Their docs also warn that API calls from server-side code may be blocked unless you use a paid plan +
#   IP safelist. If `/api/contact` starts returning errors or mail never arrives, switch to client-side only:
#   remove `VITE_CONTACT_SUBMIT_URL` from Netlify, set `VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY` for builds, redeploy.
# Do not set VITE_CONTACT_SUBMIT_URL in local `.env.development` unless you use `netlify dev`.

# Optional: custom FormAction instead of Web3Forms (advanced)
# VITE_CONTACT_FORM_ACTION=

# --- Visit section ---
# Use | between lines when a single .env line is easier (or use real newlines if your editor supports multi-line env values).
VITE_ADDRESS_LINES=RS Library,Radha Nagar, Near Dav Field | Bulandshahr, Uttar Pradesh, India
VITE_HOURS_LINES=Mon–Sat: 7:00 AM – 9:00 PM | Sun: Closed
VITE_FEE_NOTE=Ask at the desk for current daily / monthly seating rates.

# tel: link (include country code). If omitted, VITE_WHATSAPP is used for Call + WhatsApp.
VITE_PHONE=+918630849602
VITE_PHONE_DISPLAY=+918630849602

# WhatsApp: digits only with country code → floating button + Visit card link.
# If omitted, the app uses VITE_PHONE digits for wa.me when possible.
VITE_WHATSAPP=+918630849602

# Map: VITE_MAP_QUERY is used for the “Open in Google Maps” link.
# For an inline map iframe, paste the full embed URL from Google Maps → Share → Embed a map:
# VITE_MAP_EMBED_URL=https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=...

# --- Optional site extras ---
# Banner under the header (dismissible for the session). Use | between lines.
# VITE_ANNOUNCEMENT=AC maintenance Tue 2–4 PM — other hours normal.|Carry your own water bottle.

# Footer social / map links: Label~URL pairs separated by | (tilde between label and URL)
# VITE_SOCIAL_LINKS=Instagram~https://www.instagram.com/yourpage|Google Maps~https://maps.google.com/...
